                    We are seeking an engaging and experienced online tutor for two students in Years 4 and 7. The ideal candidate can confidently support English, Mathematics, and Science and has experience with an IB, Cambridge, British, Australian, American, or comparable international curriculum.



We are looking for one reliable all-round tutor who can adapt lessons to each child’s level, explain concepts clearly, and make learning enjoyable.



Required schedule — Dubai time (GST, UTC+4):

• Monday to Friday: 4:00 pm–6:00 pm

• Saturday: 12:00 pm–2:00 pm

• Total: 12 hours per week



This is a part-time, long-term online tutoring role. Lessons will be delivered live using video conferencing and shared digital learning tools. The tutor should be organised, patient, engaging, and able to prepare appropriate lesson activities, short practice tasks, and progress updates for a parent.



Please apply only if you can demonstrate:

• Teaching or tutoring experience with primary and lower-secondary students, especially Years 4 and 7 or equivalent;

• Strong capability in English, Maths, and Science;

• Experience with an international curriculum — please state the curriculum, subjects, and years taught;

• Strong spoken and written English;

• Availability for the stated Dubai-time schedule;

• A reliable internet connection and professional online teaching setup.



In your application, include:

1. The subjects and year levels you teach confidently;

2. Your curriculum experience and teaching qualifications;

3. A brief summary of your recent tutoring or classroom experience;

4. Your requested hourly rate and rate for the 12-hour weekly schedule;

5. Confirmation of availability in Dubai time;

6. A short outline of how you would structure a first lesson;

7. The phrase "Dubai Primary Tutor" at the beginning of your application.



Compensation is negotiable based on experience, qualifications, and curriculum knowledge. Shortlisted applicants will be asked to complete a paid trial lesson using age-appropriate material.

                    We are seeking an experienced online academic tutor for two students in Years 10 and 11. The ideal candidate can support Mathematics, English, Biology, Chemistry, and Physics and is confident teaching an IB, IGCSE, GCSE, A-Level, or comparable international curriculum.



We would ideally like one strong all-round tutor. However, experienced subject specialists are also welcome to apply if they can clearly state the subjects and year levels they can teach.



Required schedule — Dubai time (GST, UTC+4):

• Monday to Friday: 4:00 pm–6:00 pm

• Saturday: 12:00 pm–2:00 pm

• Total: 12 hours per week



This is a part-time, long-term online tutoring role. Lessons will be delivered live online using video conferencing and shared digital learning tools. The tutor should be organised, patient, engaging, and able to explain difficult concepts clearly. They should prepare lessons, set and mark short practice tasks where helpful, track progress, and communicate professionally with a parent.



Please apply only if you can demonstrate:

• Relevant tutoring or classroom-teaching experience for secondary students, particularly Years 10–11 or equivalent;

• Experience with IB, Cambridge/IGCSE, GCSE, A-Level, or another international curriculum — state the programme, subjects, and years taught;

• Strong spoken and written English;

• Current availability for the Dubai-time schedule above;

• A reliable internet connection and a professional online teaching setup.



In your application, include:

1. The subjects and year levels you can teach confidently;

2. Your relevant curriculum and examination-preparation experience;

3. Teaching qualifications, degree(s), licences, and a short summary of recent tutoring work;

4. Your requested hourly rate and rate for the 12-hour weekly schedule;

5. Confirmation of your availability in Dubai time;

6. A brief outline of how you would approach a first lesson in one of your strongest subjects;

7. The phrase "Dubai Secondary Tutor" at the start of your application.



Compensation is negotiable and based on relevant experience, curriculum expertise, and subject coverage. Shortlisted applicants will be asked to complete a paid trial lesson using age-appropriate material.
